{# IN·16 — the way IN to the report flow, on the dashboard.

   THE ENTRY CARD, NOT THE FORM. What it surfaces is the ruled quick-file
   discipline — a kind, one line saying what happened, a place, and nothing else
   required — so a person reads the price of filing before they start. The form
   itself lives on one route, in one set of step partials, and is not duplicated
   here: a second, shorter form would be a second product.

   IT OPENS THE FULL PAGE, NEVER THE DRAWER. The container follows the entry
   point, and the test is whether the filing came FROM A RECORD. Nothing on a
   dashboard is the record being filed about — the register behind it is a
   listing, not a source — so this is standalone filing: there is nothing for a
   drawer to sit over and nothing to inherit a place, a time or a note from. A
   page reloads, deep-links, prints, and no click beside it can throw a
   half-written report away. See templates/report/show.html.twig.

   THE LAST FILING IS CONTEXT, not a listing: "did the one I just filed land?" is
   the question somebody filing in a run actually has, and one line answers it.
   It is the newest incident in the WINDOW the page is filtered to, because every
   widget on this dashboard reads that one filter.

   The button exists only where the record routes do — a host running no security
   registers none, and a dead link into nowhere is worse than an honest line. #}
{% import '@UhifadhiIncident/dashboard/_ui.html.twig' as ui %}
{% set last = dashboard.recent is empty ? null : dashboard.recent|first %}
<div class="c" data-w="report">
    <span class="tab">File an incident<span class="src">· three answers · the rest follows on the record</span></span>
    <div class="use" style="margin:0 2px 12px">A report is cheap and a verification is expensive. Three answers and the record exists — how bad it was, who was involved, the photographs and any money are offered afterwards on the case file, where the timeline keeps who added what and when.</div>
    <div class="rln"><span><b>1</b> What kind</span><span class="mono" style="font-size:11px">{{ dashboard.categories|length }} kinds, then the sub-category</span></div>
    <div class="rln"><span><b>2</b> What happened</span><span class="mono" style="font-size:11px">one line — the register prints it</span></div>
    <div class="rln"><span><b>3</b> Where</span><span class="mono" style="font-size:11px">the place, on the map</span></div>
    <div class="rln">
        <span class="i-sub">
            {%- if last is null -%}
                nothing filed here yet — yours will be the first
            {%- else -%}
                last filed here · <a class="mono acc" href="{{ path('incident_show', {uuid: area.uuid, reference: last.reference}) }}">{{ last.reference }}</a> · {{ ui.when(last.reportedAt, dashboard.now) }}
            {%- endif -%}
        </span>
        {% if recordScreens %}
            <a class="cta" href="{{ path('incident_new', {uuid: area.uuid}) }}">{{ ux_icon('lucide:plus') }} Report an incident</a>
        {% else %}
            <span class="chip idle">filing is not enabled here</span>
        {% endif %}
    </div>
</div>
